# DNA-AND content · the grand tour: one flight from the whole visible universe down to the quarks, for watching
# Run it: Universe.exe --tour grand-tour (or DNA-AND.exe --tour grand-tour). Any key or click takes the controls back.
# Edit the stops to make your own. Each @stop is done in order:
#   do: zoom    fly in (or out, with a negative rate) steadily until the view is "until-km" across (km, the distance to what
#               you look at); rate: tenfolds a second (one steady rate, each tenfold the same time), eased in and out; a zoom
#               that stops getting anywhere for six seconds goes on to the next stop
#   do: orbit   circle slowly round what is picked (or look round if nothing is): turn degrees a second, for seconds; the view
#               is eased toward level first, so it never spins round straight up or down
#   do: look    tilt your view up (+) or down (-) by tilt degrees over seconds, turning a little as it goes
#   do: pick    choose what to go to: galaxy, next-galaxy, star, planet, next-planet, none, atom, electron, nucleus, proton, quark
#   caption:    the words shown while the stop runs
# For the eye: zoom no faster than about one tenfold in five seconds, turn no more than about four degrees a second, and
# stop to look round at each new scale, so each size can be read against the last.
# Sizes for scale: the visible universe 1.3e23 km, a web filament 1e21 km, a galaxy 1e18 km, a star system 1e10 km, Earth
# 12,742 km, a person 0.0018 km, a sand grain 2e-7 km, an atom 2e-13 km, a nucleus 1e-17 km, a proton 1.7e-18 km.

@stop leave
do: zoom
rate: -0.2
until-km: 2e22
caption: Out past the galaxies, until the visible universe shows its shape

@stop web
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 30
caption: The cosmic web: galaxies along filaments and walls, gathered in clusters, round great empty voids

@stop back-in
do: zoom
rate: 0.2
until-km: 3e19
caption: Back in, toward one strand of the web

@stop choose-galaxy
do: pick
target: galaxy
caption: A galaxy

@stop to-galaxy
do: zoom
rate: 0.18
until-km: 1.5e18
caption: Flying to it

@stop round-galaxy
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 22
caption: A galaxy of a hundred billion stars: its arms or its smooth glow, its clusters and nebulae

@stop choose-next
do: pick
target: next-galaxy
caption: On to a neighbour

@stop to-next
do: zoom
rate: 0.18
until-km: 1.5e18
caption: Across the space between galaxies, millions of light-years

@stop round-next
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 18
caption: Every galaxy is its own kind and shape

@stop into-galaxy
do: zoom
rate: 0.18
until-km: 1e16
caption: Into the galaxy, among its stars

@stop choose-star
do: pick
target: star
caption: A star

@stop into-system
do: zoom
rate: 0.18
until-km: 2e9
caption: Down to the star and its planets

@stop round-system
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 26
caption: Its solar system: the star, its planets, their moons, its belts

@stop planet-1
do: pick
target: next-planet
caption: One of its worlds

@stop to-planet-1
do: zoom
rate: 0.18
until-km: 1e5
caption: Flying past it

@stop round-planet-1
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 14
caption: A world of its own kind

@stop planet-2
do: pick
target: next-planet
caption: The next world

@stop to-planet-2
do: zoom
rate: 0.18
until-km: 1e5
caption: Across to the next world

@stop round-planet-2
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 14
caption: Each world its own size, air and ground

@stop choose-planet
do: pick
target: planet
caption: The world we go down to

@stop to-planet
do: zoom
rate: 0.18
until-km: 4e4
caption: To the planet

@stop round-planet
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 26
caption: The whole world: seas, land, clouds and air

@stop to-ground
do: zoom
rate: 0.18
until-km: 0.002
caption: Down through the air to the ground

@stop stand
do: pick
target: none
caption: Standing on the ground, six feet up

@stop look-up
do: look
tilt: 40
turn: 2
seconds: 12
caption: Looking up into the sky and space

@stop sky
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 16
caption: The sky, the star, the other worlds

@stop look-down
do: look
tilt: -75
turn: 2
seconds: 12
caption: And down to the ground at your feet

@stop to-stones
do: zoom
rate: 0.15
until-km: 1e-4
caption: The ground breaks into stones and pebbles

@stop round-stones
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 12
caption: Stones and pebbles of the ground's own rock

@stop to-grains
do: zoom
rate: 0.15
until-km: 2e-6
caption: And into grains of sand

@stop round-grains
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 14
caption: Grains of the ground's own minerals, each its own shape, colour and stains

@stop to-face
do: zoom
rate: 0.15
until-km: 2e-9
caption: Onto one grain: its steps, cracks and stains, the specks lying on it

@stop round-face
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 14
caption: A grain's face: clay plates, iron skins, a film of water

@stop to-crystal
do: zoom
rate: 0.15
until-km: 6e-12
caption: Its crystal: the atoms in their real places

@stop round-crystal
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 20
caption: The lattice, every atom held to its neighbours by shared electrons

@stop choose-atom
do: pick
target: atom
caption: One atom

@stop to-atom
do: zoom
rate: 0.15
until-km: 6e-13
caption: Into one atom

@stop round-atom
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 24
caption: An atom: its electrons in their shells round the nucleus, like a solar system; the outer (valence) shell in gold

@stop choose-electron
do: pick
target: electron
caption: One electron

@stop follow-electron
do: orbit
turn: 2
seconds: 18
caption: Following an electron, a point as far as anyone has measured, on its way round the nucleus

@stop choose-nucleus
do: pick
target: nucleus
caption: The nucleus

@stop to-nucleus
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 3e-17
caption: Across the emptiness: the nucleus is a hundred thousand times smaller than the atom

@stop round-nucleus
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 20
caption: The nucleus: its protons and neutrons, held by the strong force against the protons' electric push

@stop choose-proton
do: pick
target: proton
caption: One proton

@stop to-proton
do: zoom
rate: 0.15
until-km: 2.5e-18
caption: Into a proton

@stop round-proton
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 18
caption: A proton: three quarks, two up and one down, in the glow of the gluons

@stop choose-quark
do: pick
target: quark
caption: One quark

@stop to-quark
do: zoom
rate: 0.15
until-km: 6e-19
caption: A quark and its colour charge

@stop end
do: orbit
turn: 2
seconds: 30
caption: The smallest things known
